# S7-1500 DOL Starter Hardware Configuration

## CPU Selection - Optimized for DOL Starter Control

### Recommended CPU: S7-1516F-3 PN/DP
**Order Number:** 6ES7 516-3FN00-0AB0 (with Safety Integrated)

**Selection Rationale:**
- High performance for motor control applications
- Safety Integrated for emergency stop integration
- PROFINET for HMI/SCADA connectivity
- Sufficient I/O capacity for multiple DOL starters
- Advanced diagnostic capabilities

**Alternative CPUs:**
- **S7-1511C-1 PN:** Compact, budget-friendly option
- **S7-1513-1 PN:** Mid-range, good for single DOL starter
- **S7-1516-3 PN/DP:** High-performance, non-safety version
- **S7-1518-4 PN/DP:** Maximum performance for multiple motors

## Rack Configuration for DOL Starter

### Rack 0 (Main Rack)
| Slot | Module | Order Number | Firmware | Purpose |
|------|--------|--------------|----------|---------|
| 0 | PS 307 5A | 6ES7 307-1EA00-0AA0 | - | Power Supply |
| 1 | CPU 1516F-3 PN/DP | 6ES7 516-3FN00-0AB0 | V2.8 | Main CPU with Safety |
| 2 | SM 1231 DI 16x24VDC | 6ES7 231-4BH32-0XB0 | V2.5 | DOL Inputs + Test Inputs |
| 3 | SM 1232 DQ 16x24VDC | 6ES7 232-4HB32-0XB0 | V2.5 | DOL Outputs + Test Outputs |
| 4 | SM 1231 AI 4x13bit | 6ES7 231-4HF32-0XB0 | V2.5 | Analog Inputs (optional) |
| 5 | SM 1232 AO 2x13bit | 6ES7 232-4HB32-0XB0 | V2.5 | Analog Outputs (optional) |
| 6 | CM 1241 RS485 | 6ES7 241-1CH32-0XB0 | V2.5 | Communication (optional) |
| 7 | Empty | - | - | Reserved for expansion |

## I/O Address Assignment for DOL Starter

### Digital Inputs (SM 1231 DI 16x24VDC, Slot 2)
| Address | Tag Name | Function | DOL Starter # |
|---------|----------|----------|---------------|
| %I0.0 | DI_DOL_Start_PB | Start button | 1 |
| %I0.1 | DI_DOL_Stop_PB | Stop button | 1 |
| %I0.2 | DI_DOL_Overload | Overload relay | 1 |
| %I0.3 | DI_DOL_Aux_Contact | Auxiliary contact | 1 |
| %I0.4 | DI_DOL_Start_PB_2 | Start button | 2 (optional) |
| %I0.5 | DI_DOL_Stop_PB_2 | Stop button | 2 (optional) |
| %I0.6 | DI_DOL_Overload_2 | Overload relay | 2 (optional) |
| %I0.7 | DI_DOL_Aux_Contact_2 | Auxiliary contact | 2 (optional) |
| %I1.0 | DI_Test_Start_PB | Test start button | Test |
| %I1.1 | DI_Test_Stop_PB | Test stop button | Test |
| %I1.2 | DI_Test_Overload | Test overload | Test |
| %I1.3 | DI_Test_Contactor_FB | Test contactor FB | Test |
| %I1.4 | DI_Test_Mode_Enable | Test mode enable | Test |
| %I1.5 | DI_Manual_Contactor_Test | Manual test | Test |
| %I1.6 | DI_Reset_Test | Reset test | Test |
| %I1.7 | Reserved | - | - |

### Digital Outputs (SM 1232 DQ 16x24VDC, Slot 3)
| Address | Tag Name | Function | DOL Starter # |
|---------|----------|----------|---------------|
| %Q0.0 | DQ_DOL_Contactor | Contactor coil | 1 |
| %Q0.1 | DQ_DOL_Running_Ind | Running indicator | 1 |
| %Q0.2 | DQ_DOL_Fault_Ind | Fault indicator | 1 |
| %Q0.3 | DQ_DOL_Ready_Ind | Ready indicator | 1 |
| %Q0.4 | DQ_DOL_Contactor_2 | Contactor coil | 2 (optional) |
| %Q0.5 | DQ_DOL_Running_Ind_2 | Running indicator | 2 (optional) |
| %Q0.6 | DQ_DOL_Fault_Ind_2 | Fault indicator | 2 (optional) |
| %Q0.7 | DQ_DOL_Ready_Ind_2 | Ready indicator | 2 (optional) |
| %Q1.0 | DQ_Sim_Start_PB | Simulated start | Test |
| %Q1.1 | DQ_Sim_Stop_PB | Simulated stop | Test |
| %Q1.2 | DQ_Sim_Overload | Simulated overload | Test |
| %Q1.3 | DQ_Sim_Aux_Contact | Simulated aux contact | Test |
| %Q1.4 | DQ_Test_Mode_Active | Test mode indicator | Test |
| %Q1.5 | DQ_Test_Contactor_Out | Manual test output | Test |
| %Q1.6 | DQ_Running_Verified | Running verified | Test |
| %Q1.7 | DQ_Fault_Verified | Fault verified | Test |

### Analog Inputs (SM 1231 AI 4x13bit, Slot 4) - Optional
| Address | Tag Name | Function | Range |
|---------|----------|----------|-------|
| %IW256 | AI_Motor_Current | Motor current monitoring | 0-20mA |
| %IW258 | AI_Motor_Temperature | Motor temperature | 0-10V |
| %IW260 | AI_Voltage_Monitoring | Voltage monitoring | 0-10V |
| %IW262 | Reserved | - | - |

### Analog Outputs (SM 1232 AO 2x13bit, Slot 5) - Optional
| Address | Tag Name | Function | Range |
|---------|----------|----------|-------|
| %QW256 | AQ_Speed_Reference | Speed reference (if VFD) | 0-10V |
| %QW258 | Reserved | - | - |

## CPU Configuration Specifics

### PROFINET Interface X1
- **IP Address:** 192.168.0.10
- **Subnet Mask:** 255.255.255.0
- **Default Gateway:** 192.168.0.1
- **PROFINET Device Name:** S7_1500_DOL_Control
- **Device ID:** 0x0001

### MPI/DP Interface X2 (if used)
- **MPI Address:** 2
- **DP Master:** Yes
- **Baud Rate:** 12 Mbps
- **Highest DP Address:** 126

## S7-1500 Specific Features for DOL Starter

### Advanced Diagnostics
- **Channel-level diagnostics:** Enable for all I/O modules
- **Diagnostic alarms:** Configure for overload, wire break, short circuit
- **Maintenance alerts:** Predictive maintenance for contactors

### Safety Integration (if using F-CPU)
- **Emergency Stop:** F-input for emergency stop
- **Safety Interlock:** F-input for safety interlock
- **F-Contactor:** F-output for safety-related contactor
- **Safety Response Time:** < 50ms

### Technology Objects
- **Motor Control:** Use technology objects for advanced motor control
- **PID Control:** For process control applications
- **Positioning:** For positioning applications (if applicable)

### Web Server
- **Enable Web Server:** For remote monitoring
- **User Management:** Configure access levels
- **Web Pages:** Custom pages for DOL starter status

## System Addresses Summary

### Memory Areas
- **Digital Inputs:** %I0.0 - %I1.7 (32 points)
- **Digital Outputs:** %Q0.0 - %Q1.7 (32 points)
- **Analog Inputs:** %IW256 - %IW262 (4 channels)
- **Analog Outputs:** %QW256 - %QW258 (2 channels)
- **Merker Bits:** %M0.0 - %M1023.7 (1024 bits)
- **Timers:** T0 - T255 (256 timers)
- **Counters:** C0 - C255 (256 counters)

### Data Blocks
- **Shared DBs:** DB1 - DB100 (for global data)
- **Instance DBs:** DB101 - DB200 (for function block instances)
- **System DBs:** DB201+ (for system functions)

## CPU Performance Optimization

### Cycle Time Configuration
- **Minimum Cycle Time:** 1 ms
- **Maximum Cycle Time:** 50 ms
- **Current Cycle Time:** ~10 ms (typical for DOL starter)
- **Watchdog Time:** 5000 ms

### Interrupt Configuration
- **Hardware Interrupts:** Configure for digital input changes
- **Diagnostic Interrupts:** Enable for I/O module diagnostics
- **Time-of-Day Interrupts:** For scheduled maintenance

### Memory Optimization
- **Block Compression:** Enable for reduced memory usage
- **Optimize Block Access:** Enable for faster execution
- **Retentive Memory:** Configure for critical data retention

## Communication Configuration

### PROFINET IO Devices
- **HMI Device:** Add HMI station (if applicable)
- **I/O Devices:** Add remote I/O (if applicable)
- **Update Rate:** 1 ms for fast response
- **Watchdog Time:** 100 ms

### OPC UA (Optional)
- **Enable OPC UA:** For SCADA integration
- **Security:** Configure certificates and encryption
- **Data Access:** Expose DOL starter tags

### Modbus TCP (Optional)
- **Enable Modbus TCP:** For legacy equipment integration
- **Port:** 502 (default)
- **Data Mapping:** Configure register mapping

## Redundancy (Optional)
- **S7-1500R:** For high availability applications
- **Redundant CPUs:** Configure standby system
- **Synchronization:** Configure H-system synchronization

## Security Configuration

### Access Protection
- **Know-how Protection:** Enable to protect logic
- **Copy Protection:** Enable to bind to specific hardware
- **Access Level:** Full (for development), Read-only (for operation)

### Security Integrated
- **Safety Password:** Configure for safety-related functions
- **Safety Signature:** Configure for safety program integrity
- **F-Parameters:** Configure safety-related parameters

## Backup and Restore
- **Memory Card:** 4 GB SIMATIC Memory Card
- **Backup Frequency:** Weekly
- **Auto Backup:** Enable
- **Restore on Power Loss:** Disable (manual restore)

## TIA Portal Project Settings

### General Settings
- **Project Name:** S7_1500_DOL_Starter
- **Project Type:** Station with PLC
- **Language:** English (US)
- **Character Set:** ISO 8859-1

### PLC Settings
- **CPU Type:** S7-1516F-3 PN/DP
- **Firmware:** V2.8
- **Program Blocks:** SCL, LAD, FBD
- **Data Types:** Standard + UDTs

### Compilation Settings
- **Optimization:** Speed
- **Block Checks:** Enable all
- **Consistency Check:** Enable
- **Auto-compile:** Enable

## Testing and Commissioning

### PLCSIM Configuration
- **PLCSIM Advanced:** For advanced simulation
- **Virtual Hardware:** Configure matching modules
- **Signal Tables:** For signal simulation
- **Force Variables:** For testing

### Commissioning Checklist
- [ ] Verify hardware configuration matches physical setup
- [ ] Test all digital inputs
- [ ] Test all digital outputs
- [ ] Verify PROFINET communication
- [ ] Test emergency stop (if applicable)
- [ ] Test overload protection
- [ ] Verify all status indicators
- [ ] Test HMI communication (if applicable)
- [ ] Verify diagnostic alarms
- [ ] Document all settings

## Maintenance Considerations

### Predictive Maintenance
- **Contactor Operation Count:** Monitor for maintenance scheduling
- **Overload Trip Count:** Track for trend analysis
- **Operating Hours:** Log for maintenance planning
- **Temperature Monitoring:** For thermal management

### Spare Parts
- **CPU Spare:** Keep one spare CPU programmed
- **I/O Module Spares:** Keep spare digital and analog modules
- **Memory Card:** Keep backup memory card
- **Documentation:** Keep configuration documentation

## Documentation Requirements
- **Hardware Configuration:** Document all module assignments
- **I/O Lists:** Maintain current I/O assignment lists
- **Network Configuration:** Document IP addresses and device names
- **Safety Documentation:** Document safety-related configurations
- **Maintenance Records:** Keep maintenance and modification records
